WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:08.000
What if every architectural design took hours, not days?

00:09.000 --> 00:16.000
The problem. Thirteen core Cards domains. Hundreds of connected systems.

00:17.000 --> 00:28.000
The knowledge is scattered: ARB decisions, standards, static diagrams, expert knowledge.

00:29.000 --> 00:40.000
Every review starts from scratch. Drift is found after deployment.

00:41.000 --> 01:05.000
Today's process: Permit to Design, self-assessment, architect approval or escalation to the ARB. All of it manual.

01:06.000 --> 01:20.000
Thirty to thirty-two hours per permit. Same rigor. Without the drag.

01:21.000 --> 01:39.000
Introducing the Intelligent Architecture Factory. Five AI agents, thirteen domains, one knowledge graph. A six-to-eight-hour Permit-to-Build cycle time.

01:40.000 --> 02:29.000
One knowledge graph. Every Cards domain, always current.

02:30.000 --> 03:32.000
The Knowledge Assistant. Ask about any domain, API, or risk. Hours of digging, answered in seconds.

03:33.000 --> 04:19.000
From static pictures to Architecture-as-Code. Five specialized AI architecture agents.

04:20.000 --> 04:48.000
The same journey, automated. Design, build, deploy. Governed in hours.

04:49.000 --> 05:03.000
Transformation impact: permits from thirty hours to six, knowledge from fragmented silos to one connected graph.

05:04.000 --> 05:17.000
The future of Cards architecture: intelligent, governed, always current.
